# CODEOWNERS — mandatory reviewers by path.
# Later entries take precedence over earlier ones.
# Teams are placeholders until the GitHub organization is provisioned;
# replace @lacteva/* with real team handles when available.

# Default: documentation guild owns everything until code lands.
*                       @lacteva/docs-guild

# Standards and governance change rarely and require architecture sign-off.
/docs/00-standards/     @lacteva/architecture-board
/docs/01-governance/    @lacteva/architecture-board
/docs/02-templates/     @lacteva/architecture-board

# Architecture decisions require the architecture board.
/docs/03-architecture/  @lacteva/architecture-board

# Requirements are owned by product; software requirements co-owned by engineering.
/docs/04-requirements/business/  @lacteva/product
/docs/04-requirements/product/   @lacteva/product
/docs/04-requirements/software/  @lacteva/engineering-leads

# Contract-like documents require the owning platform teams.
/docs/06-api/           @lacteva/platform-api
/docs/07-data/          @lacteva/data-platform
/docs/08-ai/            @lacteva/ai-platform
/docs/09-events/        @lacteva/platform-api

# Root governance files.
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @lacteva/architecture-board
/CHANGELOG.md           @lacteva/docs-guild
/.github/               @lacteva/architecture-board
